Author: Peios maintainers <packaging@peios.org>
Subject: Configure without pip: use the system meson and skip the tooling group

QEMU's configure builds its Python tooling venv with mkvenv.py, which refuses
to create a venv unless ensurepip, or a system pip and setuptools, is
available, then installs pycotap and the tooling group (qemu.qmp and the
in-tree qemu package) with pip. Peios' python3 deliberately ships neither pip
nor ensurepip.

A venv over the system site-packages still finds meson and distlib there,
which is all configure and the build use. So: let mkvenv create that venv
without pip when ensurepip is absent; drop pycotap, which only `make check`'s
TAP output uses, from the meson group; and do not install the tooling group,
which serves the test and developer scripts, not the build.

Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-09-22

diff -ru a/configure b/configure
--- a/configure	2026-09-22 15:16:08.095534798 +0100
+++ b/configure	2026-09-22 15:16:26.446740785 +0100
@@ -983,11 +983,9 @@
     mkvenv_online_flag=" --online"
 fi
 
-# Unconditionally install our tooling group. PyPI is allowed if enabled here.
-
-$mkvenv ensuregroup $mkvenv_online_flag \
-        --dir "${source_path}/python/wheels" \
-        ${source_path}/pythondeps.toml tooling || exit 1
+# The tooling group (qemu.qmp and the in-tree qemu package) serves the test
+# and developer scripts, not the build, and installing it needs pip, which
+# Peios does not ship. It is not installed.
 
 # Conditionally ensure Sphinx is installed.
 
diff -ru a/python/scripts/mkvenv.py b/python/scripts/mkvenv.py
--- a/python/scripts/mkvenv.py	2026-09-22 15:16:08.098632467 +0100
+++ b/python/scripts/mkvenv.py	2026-09-22 15:16:21.272717380 +0100
@@ -247,6 +247,15 @@
                 and not need_ensurepip()
             ):
                 kwargs["with_pip"] = False
+            elif (
+                kwargs.get("system_site_packages", False)
+                and not find_spec("ensurepip")
+            ):
+                # Peios ships neither pip nor ensurepip. A venv over the
+                # system site-packages still finds meson and distlib there;
+                # only an install into the venv would need pip.
+                kwargs["with_pip"] = False
+                self.want_pip = False
             else:
                 check_ensurepip()
 
diff -ru a/pythondeps.toml b/pythondeps.toml
--- a/pythondeps.toml	2026-09-22 15:16:08.096657779 +0100
+++ b/pythondeps.toml	2026-09-22 15:16:23.544727658 +0100
@@ -20,7 +20,6 @@
 [meson]
 # The install key should match the version in python/wheels/
 meson = { accepted = ">=1.5.0", installed = "1.11.1", canary = "meson" }
-pycotap = { accepted = ">=1.1.0", installed = "1.3.1" }
 
 [meson-rust]
 # The install key should match the version in python/wheels/
